3 TEXT Joseph W. McHughBirth: Sep 3 1931Death: June 12 2010Burial: Tewksbury, MassachusettsNotes: Joseph W. McHugh of Tewksbury formerly of Stoneham, June 12, 2010. Beloved partner of Lois Needham.  Dear fri
4 CONC end and former husband of Therese McHugh.  Loving father of Joseph McHugh, Jr. and his wife Maureen of Chelmsford, Maureen M. Bigley and her husband Michael of Ayer, Kathryn M. Kendrick and her husban
4 CONC d William of Franklin, NH, Thomas R. McHugh and his fiancée Yuri-Anne Enomoto of Torrance, CA, Michael P. McHugh and his wife Patricia of Reston, VA, William F. McHugh and his wife Sharon of Harvard,
4 CONC  Rosanne L. Fluet and her husband Dennis of Mount Vernon, NY.  Cherished grandfather of 12.  Dear  brother of William McHugh, Robert McHugh,  Kathryn Hastings all of PA, James McHugh of NJ and the lat
4 CONC e Rita Weik, John and Charles McHugh.  Funeral from the Barile Family Funeral Home, 482 Main St. (RT 28) STONEHAM  Friday at 10 am followed by a Funeral Mass celebrating Joseph&#039;s life in St. Patr
4 CONC ick Church, 71 Central St., Stoneham at 11 am.  Family and friends are cordially invited to gather and share remembrances with the Family on Thursday from 4-7 pm in the Funeral Home.  Parking attendan
4 CONC ts will be available.  Interment St. Mary&#039;s Cemetery, Tewksbury.  In lieu of flowers please honor Joseph by making donations in memory of him to Doctors without Borders, PO Box 5030, Hagerstown, 
4 CONC MD 21741 or The Charity of Your Choice.
